body:
Hi @pmcelhaney, thanks for making a great repo. It helps me a lot.

After some time I used, I found an error when generating a mock when my headers contain `-`. For example: `X-AUTHORIZATION`.  Maybe you have any solution for this without making changes in the repo? Thank you.

This is the example of the header that I used : 
```
{
  "parameters": [
    {
      "in": "header",
      "name": "X-TIMESTAMP",
      "description": "e.g 2020-01-01T00:00:00+07:00",
      "required": true,
      "schema": {
        "type": "string",
        "maxLength": 25,
        "minLength": 25
      }
    },
    {
      "in": "header",
      "name": "X-CLIENT-KEY",
      "description": "Please use your client id",
      "required": true,
      "schema": {
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    {
      "in": "header",
      "name": "Private-Key",
      "description": "Please use your private key to get valid rsa key",
      "required": true,
      "schema": {
        "type": "string"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

